Title: Hypercholesterolemia as a Causal Risk Factor for COPD: Biomarker Discovery and Therapeutic Implications From NHANES Data.
Abstract: Chronic obstructive pulmonary disease (COPD), the third leading cause of global mortality, imposes substantial socioeconomic burdens. Existing therapies, such as smoking cessation and non-invasive ventilation, primarily alleviate symptoms without arresting disease progression. Comorbidities, including cardiovascular disease and metabolic syndrome, exacerbate functional decline, yet the causal role of dyslipidemia in COPD pathogenesis remains unclear. This study seeks to establish a causal link between hypercholesterolemia and COPD while identifying potential biomarkers and therapeutic targets.

